                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I've decided to play this game after receiving a Steam Key by Groupees, as a part of an old bundle. I've watched the trailer and started playing it: I've found a little treasure of mind-bending sandbox fun!!\nYou have to play this game if you love things like The Incredible Machine/Contraption Maker, Incredipede, Crayon Physics Deluxe (and also the almost-forgotten Your Doodles are Bugged!), and all those physics-based experiences that make your brain crazy!\n\nIn King Machine (that is also the original title of a non-commercial series born in 1993 on the Acorn Archimedes, thanks to the same author Dom Camus, a.k.a. FastRam Design) you have to explore an abandoned factory, using a little maintenance robot guided by the voice of an Artificial Intelligence. You have to restart the production of this old building, and to do so you will explore many different areas and accomplish more than 50 difficult missions: this adventure will keep you busy for hours and hours. If you love creative games that let you build your own structures and machines, than this is a MUST HAVE: this little gem deserves more attention!!! The satisfaction you get when you solve a problem with a contraption that you've built after hours of experimentation is unique.\nThe game has his own mini-problems and bugs (sometimes a little annoying), but it's too addictive and intelligent!\nOVERWHELMINGLY POSITIVE!",
